Package: ha-agent
Version: @VERSION@-@RELEASE@
Architecture: all
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Bruno Silva <avlis@onurb.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/avlis/ha-agent
Depends: python3, adduser
Suggests: systemd
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Description: HAProxy agent reporting backend weight and maintenance state
 Small agent for HAProxy's agent check on Linux backends. Each probe is
 answered with a weight percentage computed from CPU headroom, i/o wait and
 available memory, each factor individually weighted: HAProxy reads the
 number as a share of the weight configured for that server, so a larger
 number means more traffic and 0% acts as a drain. For instance i/o wait
 matters more on a database server than memory usage does, which is what
 the per-factor weights are for.
 .
 Sampling runs on its own thread, separate from the thread that answers
 HAProxy, so a backend can be polled by several HAProxy instances without
 the polling itself showing up as load. When no sample can be taken the
 percentage is left out of the reply, so HAProxy keeps the weight it was
 given instead of following a number the agent can no longer support, and
 the reply is never empty, because an empty reply is an agent failure.
 .
 When /etc/ha-agent.status holds a line, that line is added to the reply,
 which lets an operator drain or park a backend locally without taking it
 offline. See the agent-check section of the HAProxy documentation.
